  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "26.1.3.37: Bug fixes found by a new unit test suite (DX.Data.EF.Tests). Fixed: any batch of two or more items threw (the transaction was committed inside the loop) and left the first items saved; a failed insert or update left entities tracked and poisoned the DbContext; a rejected update leaked its values into later reads and saves; UpdateAsync with an empty key inserted a new row; failures always reported DataMode.Create; an empty batch returned [null]; batch results only held the last item; DeleteAsync threw on database errors (now a failed result); TransactionalExecAsync did not commit work that had already called SaveChanges; EFDatabase.Execute(transactional: false) rolled back the work's own SaveChanges. Performance: one SaveChanges and one commit per batch; batch Update/Delete load all keys in one query; updates write only changed columns; GetByKey reads without tracking. Behaviour changes: batches are all-or-nothing; entities of a failed operation are detached from the context; GetByKey no longer returns tracked instances (it does not see unsaved changes on the context); UPDATE statements contain only the changed columns.\n\t\t\t26.1.3.36: Added a README.md with technical documentation, now embedded in the package via PackageReadmeFile.\n\t\t\t26.1.3.35: Rebuilt to align with the DXWeb v26.1.3 release wave and pick up the latest DX.Data/DX.Utils dependency versions (no direct DevExpress dependency in this package).\n\t\t\t23.2.3.30: Data.DataStore plus Validator and Mapper have been moved and simplified into package DX.Data\n\t\t\tBREAKING CHANGES:\n\t\t\t\tData base classes moved to DX.Data package\n\t\t\t\tDX.Data package refactored to use FluentValidation with simplyfied validation logic\n\n\t\t\t23.2.3.23: Upgraded to .NET8 and DX v23.2.3 Dropped support for .NETStandard!",
